{
 "id": "gap_awareness",
 "version": "1.7.0",
 "depends_on": [
  "intent",
  "solver_dispatch"
 ],
 "capability_keys": [
  "gap_detection",
  "file_self_concern"
 ],
 "_unhandled_instruction_note": "v1.6.0: NO MORE SILENT INSTRUCTION DEAD-ENDS. After the rule passes for a turn have run, the adapter MECHANICALLY records what happened to an instruction Message (world_adapter._record_instruction_outcome, the _answer_topic_reply/_record_self_account_gap outcome precedent): instruction_outcome='handled' iff some rule claimed the turn (the comprehended fixpoint marker) or minted a Goal comprehending it, else 'unhandled' -- a datum, not a decision. note_unhandled_instruction_gap then DECIDES an unhandled instruction is a capability gap: it files SelfConcern{source:'implicit', kind:'instruction', content:'<predicate> <content>'} (content-deduped + mint-once via instruction_gap_noted, like every gap rule here) AND mints the honest reply naming what it understood and that it filed the gap -- superseding the generic honest floor. The outcome is recorded BETWEEN rule passes (converse() runs one more comprehend() after recording), so the gap reply lands in the SAME turn. A previously-unhandled verb becomes handled by teaching a Concept{name:<verb>, instruction_route:<route>} (see comprehend_instruction v2.0.0) -- then instruction_outcome reads 'handled' and no gap is filed.",
 "_upload_vision_note": "v1.5.0: when an image upload is held but lacks vision_summary (GraphEye not run at ingest), note_upload_vision_gap files SelfConcern{kind:reply_fix, content:upload_vision_wiring} on the first attachment follow-up.",
 "_self_account_note": "v1.3.0: a SELF-account gap. When the agent understands a question is about its OWN faculty ('how does your collapse function work') but holds no account of it, the reflexive path hits the honest self floor; the adapter records that outcome mechanically (self_account_unresolved=1.0 + self_account_topic = the self-thing asked about), and note_self_account_gap DECIDES it is a gap and files SelfConcern{source:'implicit', kind:'self_account', content:<the faculty>} (content-deduped, once per message). So a self-question the agent can't yet answer becomes a gap it FINDS about itself -- surfaced by _run_self_gaps, workable through the human-gated promote pipeline -- rather than a dead-end honest shrug.",
 "_dedup_note": "v1.1.0: both minting rules carry a content-dedup guard (Not Exists a SelfConcern whose content equals this gap's content), so a NEW gap is never filed twice. v1.2.0: the agent also RETRACTS pre-existing duplicates itself (legacy gaps filed before the guard) -- retire_duplicate_gap keeps ONE survivor per content and retires the rest, BATCH-SAFE without any node-id: the survivor is Argmin over the same-content active SelfConcerns (Argmin returns exactly one element from a fixed snapshot within a pass), and a SelfConcern is retired (status='retired' + del_edge has_self_concern) iff it is NOT identity-equal (Eq compares Value::Node by id) to that survivor. A unique gap is its own Argmin survivor, so it is never retired. SCOPED to source in {implicit, explicit_report} (the auto-FOUND gaps) -- conversation-sourced SelfConcerns are the human-gated promote flow and are never auto-retired. Runs in the agent's own run_rules fixpoint -- the agent fixing its own gap list, graph-native. The surfacing reader (reflective_faculty._run_self_gaps) skips status=='retired'.",
 "description": "The agent FINDS ITS OWN GAPS, graph-natively, and files each as a SelfConcern{status:'noted'} -- the SAME node shape conversation_self_concern.json mints, so the human-gated self-improvement spine (scripts/jabberwock_daemon.py::promote_self_concern -> StandingConcern) and the surfacing reader (reflective_faculty._run_self_gaps, tests/test_self_gaps_surfacing_migrated.py) both find it. TWO mechanisms, BOTH graph rules (the DECISION is never in Python). (1) IMPLICIT gap detection -- note_unresolved_topic_gap: after the adapter mechanically records the factual outcome of an answer_topic attempt onto its Goal (world_adapter._answer_topic_reply sets outcome='resolved'|'unresolved' -- a datum, not a decision), THIS rule DECIDES that an answer_topic goal whose outcome is 'unresolved' is a knowledge gap, mints SelfConcern{source:'implicit', kind:'knowledge', content:<the topic>}, and marks the goal gap_noted=1.0 so it files exactly once. (2) EXPLICIT gap report -- note_reported_gap: an interlocutor statement/utterance that the agent has NOT yet comprehended, in which a Mention resolves (seeds/intent.json's Mention -refers_to-> Concept rule, on the held DEFICIENCY concepts seeded below) to a DEFICIENCY concept (cannot/fail/repeat/gap/limitation/stuck/unable/struggle/weakness/broken/wrong) AND a Mention resolves to a SELF-word concept (you/your/yourself/...), is COMPREHENDED as a self-referential deficiency report: it mints SelfConcern{source:'explicit_report', kind:'reported', content:<the report text>} + a confirming reply, instead of being misrouted to external-topic grounding. Recognition is graph-native (held Concepts + the referent rule), NOT a Python keyword set. Both rules use the single-anchor match (agent -has_goal-> g / agent -received-> m; NEVER ['agent','is_a','Agent'] which over-fires) and a mint-once fixpoint guard (gap_noted / comprehended), exactly like conversation_self_concern / conversation_topic_route.",
